      "writtenOn": "2016-05-16T20:33:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should call charge_manager_update_charge() unconditionally with the detected type. If special actions need to be taken to enable BC1.2 charging (and not PD / USB-C charging) then we need to modify charge_manager. We can either add a supplier parameter to board_set_charge_limit() or add a new callback like board_select_charge_supplier(). What do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "deec54a5982d5001c61de6e248b4701f749133aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "924d985c_76840a1e",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bd99955.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 320,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-16T20:36:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Basically, the idea is that we tell charge_manager about the charger we\u0027ve detected, but we don\u0027t actually charge from the port until charge_manager decides to select our port. So if we need to take special actions for BC1.2 charging only, they need to be taken from the board_select_charge_supplier() callback (or a similar callback that takes supplier parameter) because only at that point has charge_manager indicated that our port + BC1.2 charging method are active. And, we might need to do cleanup (eg. call bd99955_bc12_enable_charging(port, 0)?) if a non-BC1.2 supplier is detected + chosen.",
      "parentUuid": "924d985c_362e0236",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "deec54a5982d5001c61de6e248b4701f749133aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
